Assertions:
[STATUS label=null_userid] 400 or 422 (client validation error, not a server crash) {SPEC} (a required-field violation must be a 4xx validation response)
[BODY label=null_userid] response body does NOT contain a raw exception message, stack trace, table name, or column name {SPEC} (no internal implementation detail in a client-facing error)
[STATUS label=missing_userid] 400 or 422, same class of clean validation error as null_userid {SPEC}

[STATUS label=delete_org] 200/204 -- organization delete itself succeeds {OBSERVED}
[COUNT label=post_delete_search] totalCount reflects whether the membership row was cascade-deleted or survives as an orphan -- CURRENTLY CONFIRMED to survive: totalCount = 1 {SPEC} (confirmed defect list item 6, no cascade delete wired for OrganizationMembership on organization removal)
[DATA label=post_delete_search] the surviving membership row's organizationId still references the now-deleted <ORG_ID> and its cached organizationName is stale (the org no longer exists under that name) {SPEC} (orphan record, stale denormalized name)
[EVIDENCE] the createOrganization setup mutation's errors[] is empty (no error creating the throwaway org) {OBSERVED}

[DATA label=get_setting] defaultValue = "Approved" — a member of the setting's own allowedValues {OBSERVED} (verified live 2026-07-30 on Customer 3.1021.0-pr-312-2257: the PR-review finding D defect is FIXED; the setting no longer defaults to the dead "New" constant)
